# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Advith Projects — Environment Variables Example
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values.
# The .env file is gitignored and will never be committed to version control.
#
# DO NOT put real credentials in this file — it IS committed to the repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── EmailJS Configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these values from your EmailJS dashboard at https://emailjs.com
#
# 1. Create a free EmailJS account.
# 2. Add an Email Service (Gmail, Outlook, etc.) → copy the Service ID.
# 3. Create an Email Template → copy the Template ID.
# 4. Go to Account → API Keys → copy your Public Key.
#
# Your template should include the following variables so the email is formatted:
#   {{from_name}}       → sender's full name
#   {{from_email}}      → sender's email address
#   {{from_phone}}      → sender's phone number
#   {{contact_method}}  → preferred contact method (Phone / WhatsApp / Email)
#   {{message}}         → the project brief / message

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id_here
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key_here
